            <ArticleTitle>Live birth after transfer of a tripronuclear embryo: An intracytoplasmic sperm injection as a combination of microarray and time-lapse technology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-98</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4274/tjod.45144</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although around 1-4% of human zygotes have been found to be tripronuclear, there is little information about the subsequent development and chromosomal composition of embryos that derive from these zygotes. Herein, we report a pregnancy and subsequent delivery of a healthy newborn after the transfer of a blastocyst that developed from a tripronuclear zygote that had a euploid microarray result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
